{
  "title": "The for Loop — Repeating a Fixed Number of Times",
  "subtitle": "Automating Repetitive Tasks with range()",
  "topic": "5.1 • THE FOR LOOP",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; width: 100%;\">\n  <div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4px; width: 100%;\">\n    <div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">\n      5.1 • Fixed Iteration\n    </div>\n    <h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The <hlt>for</hlt> Loop & <hlt>range()</hlt>\n    </h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 640px;\">\n      Computers excel at doing repetitive work without getting tired. A <code>for</code> loop repeats a block of code a specific number of times!\n    </p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"lesson-ref-card\">\n    <div class=\"lesson-ref-header\">\n      <span class=\"ref-badge\">PREVIOUS KNOWLEDGE</span>\n      <span class=\"lesson-ref-title\">Connecting to Earlier Concepts</span>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"lesson-ref-desc\">\n      In earlier chapters, we wrote code line-by-line. With loops, you can run those commands hundreds of times with just 2 lines of code!\n    </p>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=2&sub=3&ref_from=1_6_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: The print() Command (Lesson 2.2) →</a>\n      <a href=\"1.html?spcl=1&lsn=3&sub=1&ref_from=1_6_1\" class=\"ref-jump-btn\">Review: Variables & State (Lesson 3.1) →</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"background: #fde047; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;\">\n    <span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n      Syntax Pattern\n    </span>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">\n      The 3 Flavors of range()\n    </h2>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 12px;\">\n      <div>1. <code>range(5)</code> &rarr; 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 (starts at 0, stops before 5)</div>\n      <div>2. <code>range(1, 6)</code> &rarr; 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 (starts at 1, stops before 6)</div>\n      <div>3. <code>range(0, 10, 2)</code> &rarr; 0, 2, 4, 6, 8 (steps by 2)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 14px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">\n      <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">for</span> i <span style=\"color: #ff7b72;\">in</span> <span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">range</span>(<span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">3</span>):<br/>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Iteration\"</span>, i)  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Prints: 0, then 1, then 2</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
}